---
/**
 * The ethics statement.
 *
 * Concrete actions, not values. "I pay my own park fees" does more work than a
 * paragraph about integrity, and it's checkable, which a value isn't.
 *
 * Deliberately says nothing about future revenue. An earlier version of the
 * about page promised there'd never be affiliate links, which was a promise
 * about money rather than about conduct, and the site's own lodging schema
 * already contradicted it. What's here is all conduct, so it stays true
 * whatever the site earns.
 *
 * Rendered on section pages, not just the method page, because that's where
 * people land from search.
 */
---
<aside class="sheet breakout my-8 px-4 sm:px-5 py-5 border-l-[9px] border-l-slate">
  <p class="label m-0">How this gets written</p>
  <p class="mt-2.5 mb-0 text-[0.96rem] leading-[1.6] max-w-[58ch]">
    I don't take free admission, tell a place I'm coming, or run paid listings.
    I call the town, not the blog. I pay my own park fees. Every fact here was
    checked by a person and says who and when. If I haven't checked it, it says
    that too.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-3 mb-0 text-[0.86rem] leading-snug text-ink-soft">
    <a href="/how-we-verify/">The full method</a>, including the ones I've got wrong.
  </p>
</aside>
